  'SNYK-JAVA-ORGBOUNCYCASTLE-18512841':
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          CVE-2026-59649 in org.bouncycastle:bcpg-jdk15on@1.68 (HIGH, CVSS 4.0 8.7). Memory
          Allocation with Excessive Size Value: UserAttributeSubpacketInputStream.readPacket()
          allocates an attacker-declared subpacket length, so importing a crafted OpenPGP public key
          can exhaust the heap. Transitive dep of artifactory-papi (papi 7.68.5 > jfrog-http-client
          7.84.7 > jfrog-crypto 7.84.7 > bcpg-jdk15on 1.68). Actual papi is provided by artifactory
          env at runtime so this is a false positive: papi is provided scope in both scanned modules
          and the distribution assembly bundles runtime scope only, so no BouncyCastle jar ships in
          the plugin. No upgrade exists: the bcpg-jdk15on artifact line was discontinued at 1.70 and
          Snyk records this CVE against range [0,) there with no fix version, so no bcpg-jdk15on
          release will ever carry the fix. The fix exists only on the maintained bcpg-jdk18on line
          at 1.85, which no artifactory-papi release reaches - papi 7.161.15 does move to
          jfrog-crypto 13.21.0 and the jdk18on artifacts, but jfrog-commons-parent 13.21.0 pins
          BouncyCastle 1.84, still vulnerable to this CVE. Not reachable: the plugin imports no
          org.bouncycastle class and performs no OpenPGP work, and the CI scan reports Reachability:
          No Path Found. Current Snyk ID as of 2026-09-14; Snyk lists exactly one ID for this CVE on
          this purl, so there is no retired generation to pair it with. The jdk18on line keys the
          same CVE as SNYK-JAVA-ORGBOUNCYCASTLE-18512835, so this entry goes inert if papi ever
          moves artifact lines.
        expires: 2026-10-14T00:00:00.000Z
        created: 2026-09-14T00:00:00.000Z
  'SNYK-JAVA-ORGBOUNCYCASTLE-18512946':
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          CVE-2026-59640 in org.bouncycastle:bcpg-jdk15on@1.68 (HIGH, CVSS 4.0 8.7). Exposure of
          Sensitive Information Through Metadata: PGPSymmetricKeyEncryptedData.getDataStream()
          throws on the repeated CFB IV bytes before MDC verification completes, giving an adaptive
          chosen-ciphertext decryption oracle. Transitive dep of artifactory-papi (papi 7.68.5 >
          jfrog-http-client 7.84.7 > jfrog-crypto 7.84.7 > bcpg-jdk15on 1.68). Actual papi is
          provided by artifactory env at runtime so this is a false positive: papi is provided scope
          in both scanned modules and the distribution assembly bundles runtime scope only, so no
          BouncyCastle jar ships in the plugin. No upgrade exists: the bcpg-jdk15on artifact line
          was discontinued at 1.70 and Snyk records this CVE against range [0,) there with no fix
          version. The fix exists only on the maintained bcpg-jdk18on line at 1.85, which no
          artifactory-papi release reaches - papi 7.161.15 does move to jfrog-crypto 13.21.0 and the
          jdk18on artifacts, but jfrog-commons-parent 13.21.0 pins BouncyCastle 1.84, still
          vulnerable to this CVE. Not reachable: the plugin decrypts no PGP data and exposes no
          decryption endpoint, imports no org.bouncycastle class, and the CI scan reports
          Reachability: No Path Found. Current Snyk ID as of 2026-09-14; Snyk lists exactly one ID
          for this CVE on this purl, so there is no retired generation to pair it with. The jdk18on
          line keys the same CVE as SNYK-JAVA-ORGBOUNCYCASTLE-18512940, so this entry goes inert if
          papi ever moves artifact lines.
        expires: 2026-10-14T00:00:00.000Z
        created: 2026-09-14T00:00:00.000Z
  'SNYK-JAVA-ORGBOUNCYCASTLE-18512973':
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          CVE-2026-59642 in org.bouncycastle:bcpkix-jdk15on@1.68 (HIGH, CVSS 4.0 8.7). Improper
          Validation of Integrity Check Value: RecipientInformation.getContentStream() authenticates
          only the DER-encoded authAttrs and never checks the content digest against the
          messageDigest attribute, so CMS AuthenticatedData content can be substituted and still
          verify. Transitive dep of artifactory-papi (papi 7.68.5 > jfrog-http-client 7.84.7 >
          jfrog-crypto 7.84.7 > bcpkix-jdk15on 1.68). Actual papi is provided by artifactory env at
          runtime so this is a false positive: papi is provided scope in both scanned modules and
          the distribution assembly bundles runtime scope only, so no BouncyCastle jar ships in the
          plugin. No upgrade exists: the bcpkix-jdk15on artifact line was discontinued at 1.70 and
          Snyk records this CVE against range [0,) there with no fix version. The fix exists only on
          the maintained bcpkix-jdk18on line at 1.85, which no artifactory-papi release reaches -
          papi 7.161.15 does move to jfrog-crypto 13.21.0 and the jdk18on artifacts, but
          jfrog-commons-parent 13.21.0 pins BouncyCastle 1.84, still vulnerable to this CVE. Not
          reachable: the plugin processes no CMS or PKCS#7 messages, imports no org.bouncycastle
          class, and the CI scan reports Reachability: No Path Found. Current Snyk ID as of
          2026-09-14; Snyk lists exactly one ID for this CVE on this purl, so there is no retired
          generation to pair it with. The jdk18on line keys the same CVE as
          SNYK-JAVA-ORGBOUNCYCASTLE-18512967, so this entry goes inert if papi ever moves artifact
          lines.
        expires: 2026-10-14T00:00:00.000Z
        created: 2026-09-14T00:00:00.000Z
  'SNYK-JAVA-ORGBOUNCYCASTLE-18513024':
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          CVE-2026-59639 in org.bouncycastle:bcpkix-jdk15on@1.68 (HIGH, CVSS 4.0 8.7). Improper
          Verification of Cryptographic Signature: CMSSignedData.verifySignatures() returns true on
          loop completion without requiring any signer, so a degenerate SignedData with an empty
          signerInfos set makes unsigned content appear authentic. Transitive dep of
          artifactory-papi (papi 7.68.5 > jfrog-http-client 7.84.7 > jfrog-crypto 7.84.7 >
          bcpkix-jdk15on 1.68). Actual papi is provided by artifactory env at runtime so this is a
          false positive: papi is provided scope in both scanned modules and the distribution
          assembly bundles runtime scope only, so no BouncyCastle jar ships in the plugin. No
          upgrade exists: the bcpkix-jdk15on artifact line was discontinued at 1.70 and Snyk records
          this CVE against range [0,) there with no fix version. The fix exists only on the
          maintained bcpkix-jdk18on line at 1.85, which no artifactory-papi release reaches - papi
          7.161.15 does move to jfrog-crypto 13.21.0 and the jdk18on artifacts, but
          jfrog-commons-parent 13.21.0 pins BouncyCastle 1.84, still vulnerable to this CVE. Not
          reachable: the plugin verifies no CMS or PKCS#7 signatures - its only crypto surface is
          SSLConfiguration, which uses JDK-native javax.net.ssl and java.security only - and the CI
          scan reports Reachability: No Path Found. Current Snyk ID as of 2026-09-14; Snyk lists
          exactly one ID for this CVE on this purl, so there is no retired generation to pair it
          with. The jdk18on line keys the same CVE as SNYK-JAVA-ORGBOUNCYCASTLE-18513021, so this
          entry goes inert if papi ever moves artifact lines.
        expires: 2026-10-14T00:00:00.000Z
        created: 2026-09-14T00:00:00.000Z
  'SNYK-JAVA-ORGBOUNCYCASTLE-18519220':
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          CVE-2026-12802 in org.bouncycastle:bcpkix-jdk15on@1.68 (HIGH, CVSS 4.0 8.7). Improper
          Validation of Integrity Check Value: CMS AuthEnvelopedData recipient processing takes the
          AEAD tag length from the attacker-controlled GCM/CCM ICV length with no minimum-length
          check, making tag forgery tractable at e.g. 32 bits. Transitive dep of artifactory-papi
          (papi 7.68.5 > jfrog-http-client 7.84.7 > jfrog-crypto 7.84.7 > bcpkix-jdk15on 1.68).
          Actual papi is provided by artifactory env at runtime so this is a false positive: papi is
          provided scope in both scanned modules and the distribution assembly bundles runtime scope
          only, so no BouncyCastle jar ships in the plugin. No upgrade exists: the bcpkix-jdk15on
          artifact line was discontinued at 1.70 and Snyk records this CVE against range [0,) there
          with no fix version. The fix exists only on the maintained bcpkix-jdk18on line at 1.85,
          which no artifactory-papi release reaches - papi 7.161.15 does move to jfrog-crypto
          13.21.0 and the jdk18on artifacts, but jfrog-commons-parent 13.21.0 pins BouncyCastle
          1.84, still vulnerable to this CVE. Not reachable: the plugin processes no CMS
          AuthEnvelopedData, imports no org.bouncycastle class, and the CI scan reports
          Reachability: No Path Found. Current Snyk ID as of 2026-09-14; Snyk lists exactly one ID
          for this CVE on this purl, so there is no retired generation to pair it with. The jdk18on
          line keys the same CVE as SNYK-JAVA-ORGBOUNCYCASTLE-18519217, so this entry goes inert if
          papi ever moves artifact lines.
        expires: 2026-10-14T00:00:00.000Z
        created: 2026-09-14T00:00:00.000Z
  'SNYK-JAVA-COMGITHUBJAVAJSONTOOLS-19644208':
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          CVE-2026-86321 in com.github.java-json-tools:jackson-coreutils@2.0 (HIGH, CVSS 4.0 8.7).
          Server-side Request Forgery: JsonLoader.fromURL() fetches any URL without validation, and
          JacksonUtils.newMapper() enables WRITE_BIGDECIMAL_AS_PLAIN so an unbounded BigDecimal can
          be used for memory amplification. Transitive dep of artifactory-papi (papi 7.68.5 >
          artifactory-utils 7.68.5 > jfrog-utils > json-patch 1.13 > jackson-coreutils 2.0). Actual
          papi is provided by artifactory env at runtime so this is a false positive: papi is
          provided scope in both scanned modules and the distribution assembly bundles runtime scope
          only, so no java-json-tools jar ships in the plugin. No upgrade exists: jackson-coreutils
          2.0 is the newest release on the line and Snyk records this CVE against range [0,) with no
          fix version, so no released version is fixed. Upstream is abandoned - jackson-coreutils
          2.0 and its only consumer json-patch 1.13 were both last published in May 2020 - so no
          newer json-patch or artifactory-papi release can pull a fixed jackson-coreutils. Not
          reachable: the plugin performs no JSON Patch processing and never calls
          JsonLoader.fromURL(), and the CI scan reports Reachability: No Path Found. This finding is
          still inside its remediation SLA today and is not yet blocking; it is included here so it
          does not block a later PR for the same rationale. Current Snyk ID as of 2026-09-14; Snyk
          lists exactly one ID for this CVE on this purl, so there is no retired generation to pair
          it with.
        expires: 2026-10-14T00:00:00.000Z
        created: 2026-09-14T00:00:00.000Z
